<title>FINLAND: ATHLETICS-ENQUIST SETS INDOOR HURDLES WORLD MARK.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-ENQUIST SETS INDOOR HURDLES WORLD MARK.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPERE, Finland 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swede Ludmila Enquist set a 100 metres hurdles indoor world best time of 12.64 seconds at an international athletics meeting on Monday.</p>
<p>The Olympic champion improved the unconfirmed 12.91 set by Eva Sokolova of the then Soviet Union in St Petersburg in 1988 and the official 13.12 recorded by former East German Annelise Ehrhardt in Berlin in 1976.</p>
